  "conclusion": "The default SharedChannel path now writes const payloads of 64 KiB or more as prefix+payload slices instead of copying them into a queued staging allocation. It is 15.9% faster than the historical staged path and 3.8% faster than explicit caller-prefix borrowed storage in the same persistent 256-KiB shape. Small messages keep the staged path."
